We have derived a new existence and uniqueness theorem for a specific type of elliptic system of equations given in the paper "Existence and Uniqueness Theorem for an Elliptic System of Equations with Nonlocal Boundary Conditions." This theorem applies to a system of equations described by the equations

\begin{equation}
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
M_i(u_i,x)+\sum_{j=1}^{m}a_{ji}(x)u_j=f_i(x) \quad \text{in} \ \Omega, \\
u_i|\partial \Omega=g_i|\partial \Omega,
\end{array}
\right.
\end{equation}
where $M_i$ represents the Laplace operator and the integro-partial differential operator, and the solution exists under specific conditions related to the integro-partial differential operator's behavior at the boundary.
